{
  "dom_id": "step-q79650",
  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "Find the greatest common divisor of $1\\,722$ and $533.$",
  "worked_solution": "We use the Euclidean algorithm, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}1\\,722 & = & 533(3) & + & 123 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 533 & = & 123(4) & + & 41 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 123 & = & 41(3) & + & 0\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe last positive remainder is $41.$ Therefore, we conclude that the greatest common divisor of $1\\,722$ and $533$ is $41.$ Symbolically, we write\n\n$$\n\\text{gcd}(1\\,722,533)=41.\n$$",
